cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  CAN-Guard: machine-learning intrusion detection for
  automotive CAN-bus networks
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - name: i5 Designs
repository-code: https://github.com/yourname/can-guard
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-09-12'
keywords:
  - intrusion detection
  - automotive security
  - CAN bus
  - anomaly detection
  - autoencoder
  - operational technology
abstract: >-
  CAN-Guard detects attacks on an automotive Controller Area
  Network by combining message-timing statistics, frame-integrity
  checks and vehicle-physics consistency. A TensorFlow autoencoder
  trained only on attack-free traffic establishes a behavioural
  baseline for unseen attacks, while supervised Scikit-learn and
  TensorFlow models classify known ones. The repository includes a
  physics-based vehicle and bus simulator that generates the
  training traffic, so the whole pipeline reproduces offline with
  no proprietary data.
